    "description": "Halloween started as Samhain, the Gaelic night when the wall between worlds got thin.\nBonfires, food for the spirits and costumes to hide in. The Church's All Saints' Day on 1 November made the night before All Hallows' Eve. Soul cakes and guising became trick-or-treating, carried to America by Irish and Scottish immigrants in the 1800s.",
